Package: scAnalysisToolkit
Title: Comprehensive Toolkit for Single-Cell Multi-Omics Analysis
Version: 0.12.1
Authors@R:
    person("Eduard", "Ansaldo", , "EAnsaldo@scripps.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides a comprehensive suite of analysis and visualization tools and
    helper functions for single-cell RNA-seq, single-cell VDJ, and single-nuclei
    ATAC-seq analysis workflows. Includes helper tools/wrappers for clustering, cell
    type annotation with SingleR, differential expression analysis (pseudobulk,
    Wilcoxon, bulk RNA-seq), differential accessibility analysis, pathway enrichment,
    T-cell receptor repertoire analysis, cell-cell communication analysis with
    CellChat, motif enrichment, cNMF gene program analysis, and advanced
    visualizations including volcano plots, scatterplots, heatmaps, and circos
    diagrams. Designed to streamline end-to-end single-cell analysis with consistent
    analysis, visualization and automated output generation, enabling iterative
    frictionless analysis of datasets. It builds on functionality provided by
    single cell analysis packages such as Seurat, Signac, and others such as SingleR,
    DESeq2, CellChat. It operates with Seurat objects in R only (no support for scran
    or scanpy).
